  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\left|z^2-1\\right|=|z|^2+1$, then $z$ lies on"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\nthe real axis\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nan ellipse\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\na circle\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nthe imaginary axis.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left|z^2-1\\right|^2=\\left(|z|^2+1\\right) \\Rightarrow\\left(z^2-1\\right)\\left(\\bar{z}^2-1\\right)=|z|^4+2|z|^2+1$\n$\\Rightarrow z^2+\\bar{z}^2+2 z \\bar{z}=0 \\Rightarrow z+\\bar{z}=0$\n$\\Rightarrow R(z)=0 \\Rightarrow z$ lies on the imaginary axis."
  }
}